 "legs_note": "v4 legs = original v2 leg art; only pixels within ~6 px of the hip/knee/ankle pivots were rebuilt (round caps, outline removed on covered ends, filled by cloning the part's own v2 pixels; boot cuff widened 1 px over the trouser; instep pixels moved from shin to foot). Torso: dark trouser rows under the skirt moved to the thighs and the skirt bottom edge outlined. Generated by src/legs_v4.py from the v2 backup.",
 "build_order": "build_v2.py writes the raw v2 parts, then runs legs_v4.py (v4 joint polish) and split_pelvis_v5.py (torso/pelvis split) on that output (pass --raw-v2 to skip both); then run verify_v2.py, legs_compare.py and hip_split_check.py.",
 "root_bone": "pelvis",
 "split_note": "v5: the v4 torso PNG was split at the belt top (torso-local row 40, rest-canvas y 58) into torso (neck to belt top, 34x40) and pelvis (belt + skirt, 34x36). Pure crop of the v4 pixels; the pelvis repeats the 3 tunic rows above the cut (copied from the same image) as hidden overlap under the torso. pelvis is the root bone at the old root point; torso hangs from pelvis.waist; thighs from pelvis.hip_l/hip_r. Rest pose is pixel-identical to v4. z: pelvis took the old torso value, parts that were above the torso moved +1. Generated by src/split_pelvis_v5.py."
}
